course: dictionary
lesson: 7700
title: Provisional: for now, not final
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Provisional means for now. It is not final, and it may change later. «The Republic of China was declared in 1912, with Sun Yat-sen as provisional president.» He led the new country for now, while things were still being decided, so provisional means temporary.
explain: Use the clues around the word. The sentence says the republic was declared and Sun Yat-sen was its first president, but provisional tells you this was a temporary start, not a permanent arrangement. Swap in temporary and check: «Sun Yat-sen was its first, temporary president» still makes sense.
explain: Some words have a special meaning in one place. In the UK, a provisional driving licence is the first licence a learner driver gets, and learners show L plates on their cars. The context tells you which meaning is right.
fact: Provisional means for now, not final, and likely to change later.
fact: «Provisional» can describe a date, results, plans, or even a leader.
fact: In the UK, a provisional driving licence is the first licence a learner driver gets.
fact: «The Republic of China was declared in 1912 with Sun Yat-sen as provisional president.»
fact: Provisional is an adjective. Provisionals, as a noun, is rare.
exercise: «The Republic of China was declared in 1912, with Sun Yat-sen as provisional president.» What does provisional mean here? | *For now, not final | Sleepy and tired | Permanent, for ever | Very famous
exercise: Ellie is a learner driver in the UK and has a provisional licence. What is a provisional licence? | A prize for good driving | A licence for a lorry only | A licence that never ends | *The first licence a learner driver gets
exercise: «In 1911 an uprising in the city of Wuchang toppled the Qing.» Find and copy one word that means overthrew. | uprising | city | *toppled | Wuchang
test: «Sun Yat-sen was its first, provisional president.» Why does provisional suggest his role was not permanent? | Because he was very old | Because he was the only president ever | Because he was very tall | *Because the role was temporary and could change
test: The school says the sports day date is provisional. What does this tell you? | The sports day is cancelled for ever | The date is for now and may change | *The date is certain and can never change | The date is in the past
exam: Which word could replace provisional in «Sun Yat-sen was its first, provisional president»? | Permanent | *Temporary | Sleepy | Famous
